.TH elfshaker 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker \- Store and restore deduplicated snapshots of a working directory.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker\fR [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
elfshaker stores snapshots of the current working directory in a separate data directory. Snapshots may remain loose or be combined into compressed packs.
.PP
Commands that restore files write to the working directory. \-\-data\-dir only selects the data directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
elfshaker\-extract(1)
Restore a snapshot into the working directory.
.TP
elfshaker\-store(1)
Store files from the working directory as a loose snapshot.
.TP
elfshaker\-list(1)
List snapshots in known pack indexes.
.TP
elfshaker\-list\-packs(1)
List pack indexes known to the data directory.
.TP
elfshaker\-list\-files(1)
List files recorded in a snapshot.
.TP
elfshaker\-pack(1)
Combine loose snapshots into a compressed pack.
.TP
elfshaker\-show(1)
Write files from a snapshot to standard output.
.TP
elfshaker\-find(1)
Search snapshot tags in known pack indexes.
.TP
elfshaker\-gc(1)
Delete redundant loose snapshots and unreferenced loose objects.
.TP
elfshaker\-update(1)
Refresh indexes for all configured remotes.
.TP
elfshaker\-clone(1)
Create a working directory configured from a remote index.
.TP
elfshaker\-explode(1)
Materialize a pack\*(Aqs objects in the loose\-object store.
.SH VERSION
v1.0.0\-rc1
